+/*!
+    \since 6.13
+
+    Makes the next query check the MIME type definition files for changes.
+
+    QMimeDatabase checks the locations searched for MIME definitions for
+    changes at most once every five seconds, so a change
+    made on disk by the application, for example by installing an XML file or
+    running \c update-mime-database, is not seen until that time has passed.
+    Call this function after making such a change so that the next query
+    checks the files at once, as if the periodic check were due.
+
+    This function does not read any files itself. Since all QMimeDatabase
+    objects share the same database, it affects every one of them.
+
+    \note A binary cache file (\c mime.cache) is reloaded only when its
+    modification time is newer than the one of the file that was loaded. If
+    the cache file is regenerated within the timestamp resolution of the file
+    system, the change may not be detected.
+*/
+void QMimeDatabase::reload()
+{
+    auto *d = QMimeDatabasePrivate::instance();
+    QMutexLocker locker(&d->mutex);
+    d->requestCheck();
+}
